{"id": "clm:eb24cfbdf3a1142e1a35fc45a28ade1b14b544c421d68e06e62afd25ff0e0318", "type": "statement", "text": "Periodic per-key sensor summaries are a practical Atlas pattern: group measurements inside each window and compute averages, minima and maxima. A public smart-grid demo uses daily tumbling windows, while MongoDB's tutorial illustrates minute-scale rollups. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://dev.to/mongodb/aggregate-streaming-data-within-windows-of-time-using-atlas-stream-processing-1lm1", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Tumbling Windows"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "definition", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://github.com/ramonfnasc12/smart-grid-kafka-atlas"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:06d791e331993590edea5e794d4296b2c6581f0d0d70f49f094ef5ed949dfd6e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:1d0b25375babdb9a5444af4f92a578b789a0c6355feba9a1d87b0326759cd06d", "ev:dbc9fa59ca285be8d0b16b9843910f0c8001311b496d58ec69c39fc62174d405"]}
{"id": "clm:848172cd975b15e03400d448ff301fd90d9d611b6a50b6939ac199e0a4cf2786", "type": "statement", "text": "For event-time tumbling windows, interval duration alone does not establish wall-clock output latency. Watermark progress controls closure, and allowedLateness delays closure relative to that watermark while permitting newer windows to open. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/atlas-stream-processing/sp-agg-tumbling.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Tumbling Windows"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "structure", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/atlas-stream-processing/architecture.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:06d791e331993590edea5e794d4296b2c6581f0d0d70f49f094ef5ed949dfd6e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:0da6542a9705bbfa653fb3f5f3700b52ddc27a8eb735e40c9085d916e6ffccf9", "ev:42a66ccbf1a0626a39ab6e9ebcbfe5332289a9b4cd08f07dd3451e60a3f89091"]}
{"id": "clm:9b8be3f0e1c1a2775380c4afc62fbfb1d7f74de17105d060e72325c9eba28f71", "type": "statement", "text": "Non-overlap describes window membership. It does not establish exactly-once end-to-end delivery, guarantee inclusion of arbitrarily late events, or guarantee an output every interval of wall-clock time. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/atlas-stream-processing/windows.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Tumbling Windows"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "structure", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/atlas-stream-processing/architecture.md", "https://scotty.stream/paper/verwiebe_vldbj2023.pdf"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:06d791e331993590edea5e794d4296b2c6581f0d0d70f49f094ef5ed949dfd6e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:0da6542a9705bbfa653fb3f5f3700b52ddc27a8eb735e40c9085d916e6ffccf9", "ev:2673743bebea3d13a78ff33842266f7f5db219dd7fbb43a6addbe556d39d6fe6", "ev:626f6ac15e8539f636762e55242fbb339e2a01e8df2ca47ca24252cadffdca06", "ev:81543876fd1bf60fab9c75a5d5e4def73ca129f63339d709cc10363ae5d1961a"]}
{"id": "clm:4ebc0898c318b624991452d139e8766803ec0ac07e1d868a6261a9020eb70e99", "type": "statement", "text": "Atlas supports event-time and processing-time boundaries. Event time uses document timing; processing time uses the server clock when the processor consumes a document. A delayed event can therefore fall into different windows under the two modes. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/atlas-stream-processing/sp-agg-tumbling.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Tumbling Windows"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "mechanism", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/atlas-stream-processing/architecture.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:06d791e331993590edea5e794d4296b2c6581f0d0d70f49f094ef5ed949dfd6e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:81543876fd1bf60fab9c75a5d5e4def73ca129f63339d709cc10363ae5d1961a"]}
{"id": "clm:38a268f010336c5b15b11e9b6aba37e3f29f7cda0d4f2212112b4615b8f0bad0", "type": "statement", "text": "An idle source can leave an event-time window waiting for watermark progress. Atlas provides idleTimeout to allow windows to close during source inactivity; the stage reference and architecture guide disagree about exactly when its timer begins. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/atlas-stream-processing/sp-agg-tumbling.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Tumbling Windows"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "mechanism", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/atlas-stream-processing/architecture.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:06d791e331993590edea5e794d4296b2c6581f0d0d70f49f094ef5ed949dfd6e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:8202f69e0f030a6479bdc637c3a4304cf48804dbeee97b730fc4a901fa117f93", "ev:c0dc8182e8d5088d2aff5c242eaad27118074f153de25f3095df956c6f7f6778"]}
{"id": "clm:acebe5137c5ee6363120c3428f3b2acd8bf4df7cfee9df8f058d05c385793620", "type": "statement", "text": "Atlas defaults boundary to eventTime. When boundary is processingTime, idleTimeout and allowedLateness cannot be configured. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-14)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/atlas-stream-processing/sp-agg-tumbling.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Tumbling Windows"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/atlas-stream-processing/architecture.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:06d791e331993590edea5e794d4296b2c6581f0d0d70f49f094ef5ed949dfd6e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:2f85ee49602340992c69dd38fea5b5feccacef8713dd06cde7cc462f9b651b4e"]}
{"id": "clm:1923ccff2d28bf429ebfdae42093ebb8b2417db514f434f040f8685e77b3f684", "type": "statement", "text": "A record that arrives after its Atlas window closes cannot be assumed to update that aggregate. MongoDB documents routing late-arriving documents to a dead letter queue when one is configured. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/atlas-stream-processing/windows.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Tumbling Windows"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/atlas-stream-processing/architecture.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:06d791e331993590edea5e794d4296b2c6581f0d0d70f49f094ef5ed949dfd6e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:81543876fd1bf60fab9c75a5d5e4def73ca129f63339d709cc10363ae5d1961a", "ev:8a4eafb8fee4d91c52a3c0d9220680dfcbfd0d40e8f8c7e060f60fef2a3088d9"]}
{"id": "clm:e005f813569fe0c1ed04d8d04e66fc686c6c66f23c14a3b417acebf712d71b31", "type": "statement", "text": "With a Kafka source, Atlas waits for all partitions to pass the watermark. An idle partition can prevent windows from closing or producing results; the architecture guide recommends the source option partitionIdleTimeout. This differs from the window-level idleTimeout option. (high confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-14)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/atlas-stream-processing/architecture.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Tumbling Windows"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://github.com/mongodb/agent-skills/blob/main/skills/mongodb-atlas-stream-processing/references/output-diagnostics.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:06d791e331993590edea5e794d4296b2c6581f0d0d70f49f094ef5ed949dfd6e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:015db7822d965fa1b12879549256de2bc2a557cbc726e43b8c8be335825a6003", "ev:8202f69e0f030a6479bdc637c3a4304cf48804dbeee97b730fc4a901fa117f93", "ev:db16a41ea79928b28d6a67489fe9418351813f9cb07dfd88569e647a3e7054d0"]}
{"id": "clm:6e389598096985227bf1d082c58860cabc1cc23cf349de159c28b25469ac7258", "type": "statement", "text": "Atlas supports only one window stage per stream processor pipeline, and a single $group key inside a window has a documented limit of 100 megabytes of RAM. These are Atlas implementation limits rather than properties of the tumbling-window model. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-14)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/atlas-stream-processing/sp-agg-tumbling.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Tumbling Windows"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:06d791e331993590edea5e794d4296b2c6581f0d0d70f49f094ef5ed949dfd6e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:a543fd1498fe83338c5bb293526f0560698dc6a0e93ed027c73a9aef723e78c2"]}
{"id": "clm:d0da8a4df68619aba299ad5c904590a47ba5e8af9ae46094210203f7e29f213d", "type": "statement", "text": "Tumbling windows partition time into fixed-duration, contiguous intervals without overlap. Each event timestamp maps to one interval; this describes assignment, not a guarantee that arbitrarily late events will be accepted. MongoDB, Apache Spark, and Confluent independently document this window model. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/atlas-stream-processing/windows.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Tumbling Windows"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://spark.apache.org/docs/latest/streaming/apis-on-dataframes-and-datasets.html", "https://docs.confluent.io/platform/current/ksqldb/concepts/time-and-windows-in-ksqldb-queries.html", "https://scotty.stream/paper/verwiebe_vldbj2023.pdf"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:06d791e331993590edea5e794d4296b2c6581f0d0d70f49f094ef5ed949dfd6e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:065d6d2fe8e1ce840dc3edf5743b55dbac73f796bca1fff087ab68b8af05213b", "ev:2673743bebea3d13a78ff33842266f7f5db219dd7fbb43a6addbe556d39d6fe6", "ev:7df5ba68e15c84e62d89c4cdc788eb195fdea3f29ff230b935da05e8b8499960"]}
{"id": "clm:475763cb0625c4888054725d77d714b500ec1a5ee31e9dcdf1761a64d36ab7d7", "type": "statement", "text": "In Atlas Stream Processing, $tumblingWindow supplies a finite set of streaming documents to its nested aggregation pipeline. This enables per-interval grouping and statistics such as averages, minima, and maxima. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/atlas-stream-processing/sp-agg-tumbling.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Tumbling Windows"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/atlas-stream-processing/windows.md", "https://dev.to/mongodb/aggregate-streaming-data-within-windows-of-time-using-atlas-stream-processing-1lm1"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:06d791e331993590edea5e794d4296b2c6581f0d0d70f49f094ef5ed949dfd6e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:0febfc0114dd16ac7c43612e5f9fa6e12852b9e2b91033e06c73b9efe9da80e2", "ev:a213ccdb3bcce5465c957d221e8ef75296d461e904eac19cab76a3cad0a8ad18"]}
{"id": "clm:0a978bcaf521f837a7d2ac8d17887e030f171cccc7b105a261a4c42698c1777f", "type": "statement", "text": "The Atlas $tumblingWindow stage requires interval and pipeline. interval.size is a positive integer, and interval.unit accepts ms, second, minute, hour, or day. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-14)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/atlas-stream-processing/sp-agg-tumbling.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Tumbling Windows"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:06d791e331993590edea5e794d4296b2c6581f0d0d70f49f094ef5ed949dfd6e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:61c5c2e906b41944625149ed7d242b741ace3252a85527003713896a0325cff0"]}
{"id": "clm:641f263d9945186381dc8459aeea8c78e0264ee77ef3ae81c3aeaa98faa740fa", "type": "statement", "text": "Atlas aligns tumbling boundaries to UTC by default and offers offset to shift them. An offset of eight hours moves the boundaries eight hours ahead of UTC; the documentation does not establish automatic daylight-saving adjustment. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-14)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/atlas-stream-processing/sp-agg-tumbling.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Tumbling Windows"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:06d791e331993590edea5e794d4296b2c6581f0d0d70f49f094ef5ed949dfd6e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:db780b0ca0f75f5906627039e70139203fc0d7af19cb6acda2b55830838d035d"]}
{"id": "clm:6c4acc0e9d98c13fcf8f6b75cffc511021e56ffe4170163e2cabeeed5f769d5d", "type": "statement", "text": "The documented default allowedLateness is 3 seconds, and zero can be supplied explicitly. This is a window-closure allowance relative to watermark progress, not a promise to include every delayed record. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-23)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/atlas-stream-processing/sp-agg-tumbling.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Tumbling Windows"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:06d791e331993590edea5e794d4296b2c6581f0d0d70f49f094ef5ed949dfd6e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:f515810ef1d6967cb5decdb9cfb1e8e42fa18eef153a790758c6da9f63889a18"]}
{"id": "clm:5ea74e4b511941d6de6ece84b7b5da2f8f278a43c0f1cfa85a133e8fbb58f648", "type": "statement", "text": "Late events do not move the fixed time boundaries of a tumbling window. They can change its aggregate if accepted while its state is retained; Atlas allowedLateness delays closure to allow this. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://scotty.stream/paper/verwiebe_vldbj2023.pdf", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Tumbling Windows"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/atlas-stream-processing/architecture.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:06d791e331993590edea5e794d4296b2c6581f0d0d70f49f094ef5ed949dfd6e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:0da6542a9705bbfa653fb3f5f3700b52ddc27a8eb735e40c9085d916e6ffccf9"]}
{"id": "clm:1715a58081a720f7955944f5eab6a544687779008c69c57fbebdd6a68b038b29", "type": "statement", "text": "Atlas preserves stateful window processing through checkpoints. After interruption, a processor resumes from its last committed checkpoint; this does not establish end-to-end exactly-once delivery to every possible sink. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/atlas-stream-processing/sp-agg-tumbling.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Tumbling Windows"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/atlas-stream-processing/architecture.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:06d791e331993590edea5e794d4296b2c6581f0d0d70f49f094ef5ed949dfd6e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:626f6ac15e8539f636762e55242fbb339e2a01e8df2ca47ca24252cadffdca06", "ev:d7d3558dd06a6094c0c4cc054296bc8ad38795a44001201a6268d0f42763302b"]}
